      "computation_change_reason": "Defines when a reported DMR value counts as evidence of limit exceedance/violation; interpretation of which averaging basis is enforceable for a given parameter directly changes whether a measurement is treated as exceeding an applicable numeric limit."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/final_permit.pdf",
      "locator": "page/section/table/footnote as given",
      "exact_span": "Other measurements of oxygen demand (e.g., TOC and COD) may be substituted for five day Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD5) or for five day Carbonaceous Biochemical Oxygen Demand (CBOD5), as applicable, where the permittee can demonstrate long term correlation of the method with BOD5 or CBOD5 values, as applicable. Details of the correlation procedures used must be submitted and prior approval granted by the permitting authority for this procedure to be acceptable. Data reported must also include evidence to show that the proper correlation continues to exist after approval.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,B",
      "computation_change_reason": "Allows alternative oxygen-demand parameters in place of BOD5/CBOD5 only under demonstrated correlation and prior approval; whether substitution is valid changes which numeric limit applies to reported values and whether substitute monitoring satisfies the underlying monitoring requirement."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/final_permit.pdf",
      "locator": "page/section/table/footnote as given",
      "exact_span": "The permittee shall report all overflows with the Discharge Monitoring Report submittal. These reports shall be summarized and reported in tabular format. The summaries shall include: the date, time, duration, location, estimated volume, and cause of the overflow; observed environmental impacts from the overflow; actions taken to address the overflow; and ultimate discharge location if not contained (e.g., storm sewer system, ditch, tributary).",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Imposes overflow reporting content and timing tied to DMR submittals; interpretation of what counts as an overflow event or required tabular fields changes whether overflow monitoring/reporting was required in FY2025 and how incomplete overflow records are classified."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/final_permit.pdf",
      "locator": "page/section/table/footnote as given",
      "exact_span": "The permittee shall report any noncompliance which may endanger health or the environment. Notification shall be made to the EPA at the following e-mail address: R6_NPDES_Reporting@epa.gov, as soon as possible, but within 24 hours from the time the permittee becomes aware of the circumstance.",
      "affected_purpose": "B,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "Creates a conditional 24-hour notification obligation keyed to noncompliance that may endanger health or the environment; different interpretations of the endangerment threshold or awareness timing change which events trigger required reporting and whether absent notifications indicate missing required evidence."
    }
  ]
}
